# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded tan(pi x) of B64
#
# With 64 x = iq + z 2^-63 for an integer iq (folded so that the table index is at most 32): tan(pi iq/64) from a
# table, tan of the small residual from an odd polynomial, combined by the tangent addition formula in
# double-double arithmetic, and an error bound says whether the sum rounds safely. When it can't, a longer
# double-double polynomial redoes it. Small |x| has its own polynomials, |x| >= 2^46 reads the table directly, and
# the inputs whose result lies too close to a rounding boundary are listed (by tan's periodicity and symmetry, in
# terms of x mod 1/2). Multiples of 1/4 are exact. Round to nearest only.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/tanpi/tanpi.c via RazorForge's B64Tanpi.rf.
# Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Alexei Sibidanov
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module System/Numerics/B64

